{
  "language": "en",
  "wordOrder": "verb-first",
  "purpose": "English has no capital letters that mark nouns and no closed list holds every verb, so M01 flags a task name only on evidence of a wrong form: one word; no word with a letter after the first (Step 3); a label prefix (SAP:); a first word from nonVerbStarters or nounStarters (The invoice, Path A); a gerund (Checking invoice); two words ending in a participle (Invoice checked); an auxiliary as second word (Invoice is checked); a noun that is also a verb before a state word (Request pending). After a first word the data names as no verb (the -ate exceptions, Certificate check) a participle, state word, verb or action noun at the end counts too. A first word that is a listed verb, a prefix plus a listed verb (reorder), a verb phrase (back up), a hyphenated word ending in a verb (Quality-check) or has a verb suffix (-ate, -ize, -ise, -ify) needs an object after it. Any other first word passes and is named in hint H14; no rule reads the verb list to find a fault, so a shorter list gives more hints, never more findings. M06 and M05 flag a name that starts with a listed verb outside nounVerbHomographs; not an event ending in a participle or state word, nor a message ending in a message noun after a verb outside instructionVerbs (Deploy request; Send invoice is flagged). Extend or trim lists with a BPMN_NAMING overlay: only the lists of its schema (here verbs, verbPhrases, nounVerbHomographs, stateWords, nounStarters, messageNouns).",
  "listNotes": {
    "questionMarks": "M02 reads it: a gateway name counts as a question when it contains one of these strings.",
    "verbs": "M01 passes a task name that starts with a listed verb and an object; an unlisted first word passes with hint H14, so the list never causes an M01 finding. M06 and M05 flag an event or message that starts with a listed word outside nounVerbHomographs; M01 flags a container that is one listed word.",
    "verbPhrases": "Multi-word verbs (back up, shut down, hand off) that may open a task name; at least one more word must follow.",
    "verbPrefixes": "Prefixes (re, pre, co) that may come before a listed verb, joined (reorder) or as a word of their own (pre approve); a joined prefix needs at least three more letters.",
    "infinitiveSuffixes": "A first word with one of these endings and the minimum length (calibrate, optimize, simplify) counts as a task verb without a list entry; an exception of the ending (certificate, template) is known as no verb, so a verb or state at the end of its name is flagged.",
    "nounVerbHomographs": "Listed verbs that are also nouns (order, request): M06 and M05 do not flag an event or message that starts with one, so \"Request for details\" passes; M01 flags a two-word task name of one and a state word (Request pending).",
    "participles": "The -ed ending plus irregular forms (sent, written), less the exceptions (need, feed): M01 flags a container, a two-word task name and M05 a message whose last word is one; M06 does not flag an event that starts with a verb but ends in one.",
    "stateWords": "State words (open, ready, complete): M06 does not flag an event that starts with a verb when its last word is one; M01 flags a two-word task name of a homograph and one (Request pending).",
    "nonVerbStarters": "Determiners, pronouns, prepositions, conjunctions and auxiliaries (the, our, for, and, is): M01 flags a task name that starts with one. A closed class, so the overlay does not change it.",
    "nounStarters": "Frequent nouns and adjectives that never open an instruction (customer, system, final) and placeholder nouns (path, option): M01 flags a task name whose first whole word is one, so Path A is flagged.",
    "auxiliaries": "Forms of be, have and do (is, are, been, has): M01 flags a task name whose second word is one (Invoice is checked), or whose second word is to and third one (Invoice to be checked).",
    "messageNouns": "Nouns that name a message (request, order, invoice): M05 does not flag a message flow whose last word is one for starting with a verb (Deploy request), unless that verb is on instructionVerbs; a participle at the end is still flagged.",
    "instructionVerbs": "Verbs that make a name with a message noun an instruction: they send the message (send, submit, transmit) or decide on it (approve, confirm, cancel). M05 flags \"Send invoice\" and \"Approve order\" although the last word is a message noun.",
    "eventMarkers": "Read by the marker inference for events (message, timer, error, signal, escalation, conditional), not by M01, M05 or M06; a keyword matches a whole word only."
  },
